id: tainted
name: Tainted
kind: conditions
# One stack per clock, so the Square stays Poisonous until the last attacker's clock runs
# out rather than the first. The cap only has to be out of anybody's reach, as Ignited's does.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry makes a Square Poisoned and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# The Environmental Quality this mark puts on the Square while it is held. Named here and
# not in the code, where no Quality is named.
quality: poisonous
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Venom soaks the ground under you. Your Square is Poisonous.
text: >
  Tainted: the Elemental (Poison) Profile's mark. "Any Squares occupied by Character(s) who
  take Damage from this Attacking Maneuver become Poisoned (see — Environmental Qualities,
  Battle Environments) until the start of your next turn."

---

# --- The name is this system's ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ignited's twin, for poison: the entry makes a Square "Poisoned", which is the Poisonous
# Environmental Quality - the Quality's file is named for the adjective, the Combat
# Condition for the participle, and the entry uses the second for both. It lands on whoever
# took the Damage, as a mark on the attacker's clock, and `qualitiesOf` adds the Quality in
# the `quality:` header while it is held.
#
# Not called Poisoned, which is the Combat Condition's own id: one name for two files would
# have the lookup return whichever loaded last.
#
# No effects of its own. What poisoned ground does is the Poisonous Quality's file.
